Qualification and monitoring reuse [Measurement Process Characterization — NIST/SEMATECH](../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Statistical-Handbook.lingua#r_6S3221KSX1KKGPJNXKC3N022NN), chapter 6; [Measurement uncertainty in conformity assessment — JCGM 106](../../inquiry/metrology/sources/GUM-Conformity.lingua#r_0VFKYJZJC8BXM2T2TSY58DD6SY); and [Systems Engineering Handbook — NASA](../../engineering/mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/sources/Systems-Engineering-Handbook-NASA.lingua#r_7ZQFZ9E1NAVG27SE2R5S24PDBQ), chapter 5.

Shared quantitative, chemical and metrology Records retain their own reading. [Cleaning equipment for oxygen service — EIGA 33/18](../../utilities/industrial-gases-vacuum-and-high-purity-supplies/sources/Cleaning-for-Oxygen-Service-EIGA.lingua#r_27WYRBCNFB89Z5DXR0PMHWNES0) provides a comparison with oxygen-service cleanliness. All books, articles and media remain external.

